# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the Hevalo admin (admin.hevalo.app).
# The admin is a self-contained Vite SPA: it loads only its own hashed
# /assets/*.js + /assets/*.css, no external fonts, and only the shop's art as
# external images (img-src, below). There is no
# edge proxy, so it calls the API on its own origin cross-origin — that origin is
# listed in connect-src below and must be kept in step with VITE_API_URL (see
# admin/src/api.ts).
#
# img-src carries the website (https://hevalo.app, where the shop's own
# backgrounds and icons are served from) and its subdomains (the media CDN that
# serves art uploaded here, CDN_BASE_URL), so the shop page can show every
# item's picture, and blob: for the preview of a picture before it is
# uploaded. If CDN_BASE_URL is ever on another domain, add it here too.
#
# style-src carries 'unsafe-inline' because React writes every inline style as
# a style attribute, and the admin sets a few (the width of a progress bar, the
# height of a chart's bar), which change with the data. Without it the browser
# blocks the attribute — not only <style> blocks — and drops the declaration
# silently: no console error unless something is listening for
# securitypolicyviolation. The same policy on the public site reported
# effectiveDirective "style-src-attr", blockedURI "inline".
#
# What that cost here: the Analytics page sizes its DAU and signup bars by
# height and its funnel by width, so all three have been rendering empty.
#
# script-src stays 'self' with no 'unsafe-inline', which is the directive
# that matters: CSS-only exfiltration needs markup injection first, and that
# is what script-src and the escaping in React already prevent.
#
# media-src and microphone=(self) are for the Alphabet audio page: an editor
# records a letter here (the microphone, on this origin only, and only after
# the browser asks them), hears it back before saving (a blob: URL), and plays
# what is already stored (the media CDN, over https). The rain behind every
# page (/backdrop/, ui/Backdrop.tsx) is the only other media, and it is this
# origin's own. Nothing else asks for either.
#
# style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline' would be tighter, but a browser without
# CSP3 attribute support falls back to style-src and silently reproduces
# exactly this bug, so it is not the safer option it looks like.
#
# connect-src names no media host. The Characters page reads each stored
# recording to make its mouth timeline, but through the API
# (GET /admin/audio/:kind/file), not from the CDN or wherever a dictionary
# pronunciation is kept: those are only ever played (media-src) or shown
# (img-src), which needs neither a connect-src entry nor CORS on their side.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://hevalo.app https://*.hevalo.app; font-src 'self'; media-src 'self' blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://kurda-api.onrender.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# The backdrop's video and still are not hashed like /assets/, so they are kept
# a day rather than a year: a new loop reaches everyone by the next morning.
/backdrop/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
